The package creates user and group _sl, the directory /var/sl
(mode 0700, owner _sl:_sl), and /etc/sl.conf (mode 0640, owner
root:_sl) from the sample.

Initialize the database as that user, then start the daemon:

# doas -u _sl slctl init
# rcctl enable sld
# rcctl start sld

Replace the admin user and password, then restart so old logins stop:

# doas -u _sl slctl passwd
# rcctl restart sld

sld does not create the database. A start before init exits before
the daemon forks. PostgreSQL is optional and needs p5-DBD-Pg, which
this package does not depend on.
